    "surface": "PowerPoint",
    "steps": "APPROACH 1 — Brand kit (simplest, best for most decks): In the Copilot pane in PowerPoint, click the + under the prompt box and choose \"Select brand\" (see screenshot below), then pick the Hugessen brand kit rather than the default themes. Generated slides pick up firm fonts and colours automatically.\nAPPROACH 2 — PowerPoint agent (for bigger or more polished builds): The PowerPoint agent in 365 Copilot is Claude-powered and can assemble a fuller deck, but it won't infer our house style on its own — so spell the brand out in your prompt: fonts, the orange accent, charcoal for text and headers, layout conventions, and any table/chart formatting rules. The more specific the brand instructions, the closer the output lands.\nAPPROACH 3 — Replicate an existing deck: Attach a recent on-brand Hugessen presentation to Copilot Chat and ask it to build your new slides using that deck's formatting as the template. A clean past deliverable is the best reference — Copilot mirrors its fonts, colours, and layout.\nWhichever route: review layout and chart formatting against our house style before anything goes to a client — Copilot gets close but rarely nails every detail.",
